  "term": "directional hypothesis",
  "definition": "A directional hypothesis is a prediction that an effect or relationship will go in a specified direction, such as expecting one factor to positively influence another. In the source study, it referred to predicting positive influences of attitudes, norms, and perceived control on intention.",
